      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-11-28_WidnesExaminer_art0028" n="art0028">
        <head>CONVICTED OF CRUELTY TO HER</head>
        <p>CONVICTED OF CRUELTY TO HER</p>
        <p>DAUGHTER</p>
        <p>HARRIERS.</p>
        <p>RUNCORN ATHLETIC. HIRRIRRS.</p>
        <p>On Saturday the above club held their first club race at Runcorn when they entertained Edgekill Congregations. Harriers. Owing to the late arrival Of the visitors it we deeided to run a voile break, for which the visitors have good reputation. The visitors were fully represented, whil Runcorn lacked the services ef twe of their most prominen runners. I Goodall and T Shallcross, The plaaings were a follows :—Runeorn Harriers : W Hulse, 2nd ; I Povey,3rd4 8 Hopkins, 4th ; Wainwrigkt, 6th ' • Filkins, 91k, total 2, points; : J Morrison, 1; W Bulge, sth; 0 Mclntosh 7th; D Wilson, Bth ; B Hewitt, 121 k, total, 33 points ; being a viotory for Ransom by nine points.</p>
        <p>If you have net already Geo. G. BOBSEY &amp; Go's. Indoor Games List, obtain it from your Dealer.</p>
