      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-11-28_WidnesExaminer_art0032" n="art0032">
        <head>LANCASHIRE COMBINATION.</head>
        <p>LANCASHIRE COMBINATION.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON! "A " WIN BY A TRY TO NIL. Warrington " A" isehleved a victory en Saturday whe a Rochdale Kornets "A were the visitors to the Wilderspoel enclosure. After a spell of attacking by the visitors Pilling- lam transferred play to centre. Bailey reoelvect the ball from Edmonds but was unable to gel over, The home team continued to press, and Duckworth score I a try which was not improved upon. The visitors now became aggressive but could mot equalise, and half time arrived with Warring- ton leading by a try to nil. Uninteresting play was witnessed daring the second half, each end being visited in turn. Shortly before the elose B4monds obtained pos- session, and after running half the length of the field trans- ferred to Fillingham. That player passed to Bailey Who spoiled what seemed a :certain score by knocking on. Binal : —Warrington" A," one try, Rochdale Hornets" A," nil.</p>
