        <p>ROCHE'S HERBAL EMBROCATION.</p>
        <p>30,000 BLIND PEOPLE</p>
        <p>HAVE HAD THEIR SIGHT RESTORED</p>
        <p>MELLOR, 168, OXFORD ST., MANCHESTER.</p>
        <p>Book Post Free on mentioning WARRINGTON EXAMINER. Read what Warrrrington People say: A WARRINGTON CASE.—RECOMMENDED BY A BOY AT THE STATION.</p>
        <p>35, Hulme-street, Dalton Bank, Warrington. Mr. Mellor, Dear Sir, —Allow me to tender my sincere thanks to you for the great benefit I received whilst under your treatment with my eyes. I was recommended to you by a little by at the station. He saw my eyes In bandages, and out of pure sympathy and a knowledge of what you had done for others, mentioned your name,to me. I came and after three (3) visits, was able to see again. You are at liberty to do with this as you think proper.—Yours truly, THOMAS FBANGLETON. A WARRINGrON CASE DISCHARGED INCURABLE FROM THE EYE HOSPITAL.</p>
        <p>20, Leonard Street, Warrington. March bth, 1897. Mr Mellor, Dear Sir,—l write to thank you for:the marvellous cure you have made of my eyesight. Previous to being recommended to you I had been a patient to the Manchester eye Hospital for over two years, and was discharged incurable. My left eye was com pletely blind, but after receiving your treatment for about seven months, my eyesight is restored, and I can see better tkaa ever. I shall be pleased to recommend your treatment to everybody that needs a cure,— I am, yours sincere (MRS.) W. SHELDON.</p>
