ent men. Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters contain not only a suitable 4usntity of Quinine in each dese,but the active principlos ef the following well-kn•vro herbs—Serial:mu- ' iffa, Saffron. Gentiao,Lavonder,Burdock,and Danclnlicn. The use of Quinine is well known, but it has never been satisfactorily combined with theme preparations, until, after overcoming considerable difficulties, the proprietor was able to secure perfectly uniform preparation.cem- bluing all the essential properties of the above plants in thijir greatest purity and concentration. It is now established as a family medioine, and is increasing in popular favour the mere it is known and tested. Gwllytn Evans' Quinine Bitters is a tonic "Pick-me-up," scientifically mixed in happy proportions. Sold everywher. in bottles 25. 9d. and 4s. fil. each. Should any difficulty be experienced in procuring Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters, it will be forwarded carriage free, for the above prices, by the Sole Proprietors The Quinine Bitters Manufacturing Company, Limited Llanelly. South Wilma. We partioularlF caution our readers against imitators, and impress mufti them the importance of always oeeise that the name et G vilrm Evans "is on the Label, Stamp, and 133ttle, without which none is genuine.</p>
