        <p>A Warrington Burning Fatality. My. S. Brighouse, County Coroner, conducted an inquest at .ng the Warrington Police Station on Satur- day, ouchl the death if Minnie Roberts aged three year% t who lived . with her parents at 26, School Brow. who sustained burns which resulted In her death in the Infirmary on the previous Tlaurs- day.—Louisa Roberts, mother of the deceased, Stated that at 7.45 onThursday morning she got Wand came downstairs, leaving deceased and her Mater, aged four, in bed. After lighting the fire, She left the house to make a email purchase for breakfast. On returning a few minutes later she found the deceased on the stairs with her cotton nightdress on fire. Witness at once put out the flames, and deceased was taken tO the Infirmary. The other child informed witness that deceased was Stirring up the lire with a poker, when her night- dress became ignited.—Nurse Garnet t said deceaeed Was admitted to the Infirmary at 8.30 on Thursday Morning suffering from severe burns on the ar ma, nee and chest, and she died at 10.45.—A verdict of Acci dental death '' Wa9 returned.</p>
